> I am getting the error:

> lavaan WARNING: small number of observations (nobs < nvar) nobs = 230 nvar = 769

That is not an error, it is a warning.

> I am curious about possible solutions to this issue.

Gather more data ;-)  Or if you have prior beliefs justified by strong theory and/or prior empirical evidence, you can use informative priors in blavaan to overcome the lack of information in your data.

https://faculty.missouri.edu/~merklee/blavaan/resources.html

> Does anyone know what Lavaan can handle if nobs < nvar

What do you mean "handle"?  It was only a warning, so it sounds like the optimizer still might have found a solution against all odds.  But it doesn't follow that you can place a lot of faith in the solution, since you are essentially trying to model more information than you actually observed.

